# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this static HTML portfolio website.

## Changes Made

### Modified Files
- **index.html** - Added Vercel Web Analytics script tag in the `<head>` section

### Implementation Details

According to the latest Vercel documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart and https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/package), I implemented Web Analytics using the recommended approach for static HTML sites:

1. **Added the CDN-hosted analytics script** just before the closing `</head>` tag:
   ```html
   <!-- Vercel Web Analytics -->
   <script defer src="https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js"></script>
   ```

2. **Script attributes**:
   - Used `defer` attribute for optimal performance (non-blocking script loading)
   - Script loads from Vercel's CDN at `https://cdn.vercel-insights.com/v1/script.js`

3. **No package installation required**: For static HTML sites, Vercel Analytics works via the CDN-hosted script tag without requiring the `@vercel/analytics` npm package.

## Why This Approach

- **Static HTML site**: This project is a pure HTML/CSS/JS portfolio site without a build process or framework
- **CDN-hosted script**: The official Vercel documentation recommends using the CDN-hosted script for non-framework sites
- **Non-invasive**: The script uses the `defer` attribute to avoid blocking page rendering
- **No dependencies**: No npm packages or build configuration needed

## How It Works

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. The analytics script will automatically track page views and visitor interactions
2. Data will be collected at `/_vercel/insights/*` endpoints
3. Analytics dashboard will show data after deployment (may take a few days for initial data to appear)

## Next Steps

After this PR is merged and deployed to Vercel:
1. Web Analytics will automatically begin collecting data
2. View analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the project's Analytics section
3. Visitor data and page views will appear within a few days

## Notes

- The implementation follows Vercel's official quickstart guide for static HTML sites
- The script is loaded with the `defer` attribute to ensure optimal page load performance
- No changes to CSS, JavaScript, or other assets were necessary
- The existing code structure and functionality remain unchanged
